      "sketch.asm": ";This program creates a continuous loop that turns \n;Port 1 pins completely ON and OFF. (To make this \n;visible on a real chip, you would normally insert \n;a delay loop between the states)\n\nORG 0000H\nHERE:\nMOV P1, #0FFH     ; Turn all pins of Port 1 HIGH (ON)\nACALL DELAY       ; Call a delay subroutine (assumed written below)\nMOV P1, #00H      ; Turn all pins of Port 1 LOW (OFF)\nACALL DELAY       ; Call delay again\nSJMP HERE         ; Short Jump back to 'HERE' for an infinite loop\n\n; --- Simple Delay Subroutine ---\nDELAY:\nMOV R3, #0FFH\nLOOP: \nDJNZ R3, LOOP     ; Decrement R3 until it hits 0\nRET               ; Return to the main program\n\nEND\n"
